{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Jethro heard.</b> What report did he hear and come? The splitting of the Sea of Reeds and the war with Amalek." "<b>Jethro.</b> Seven names were given to him: Reuel, Yeter, Yitro, Chovav, Chever, Keini, Putiel. Yeter — because he added one section in the Torah: ״וְאַתָּה תֶחֱזֶה״. Yitro — when he converted and fulfilled the commandments, they added one letter to his name. Chovav — because he cherished the Torah. Chovav is Yitro, as it says: ״מִבְּנֵי חוֹבָב חֹתֵן מֹשֶׁה״ (Judges 4). And some say Reuel was Yitro's father. Then what does it mean: ״וַתָּבֹאנָה אֶל רְעוּאֵל אֲבִיהֶן״? That little children call their grandfather 'Father.' In Sifrei." "<b>Father-in-law of Moses.</b> Here Yitro was aggrandizing himself through Moses — I am the king's father-in-law. And previously, Moses was hanging the greatness on his father-in-law, as it says: ״וַיָּשָׁב אֶל יֶתֶר חֹתְנוֹ״ (Exodus 4)." "<b>To Moses and to Israel.</b> Moses is weighted equally against all Israel (Mekhilta)." "<b>All that He had done.</b> For them in the descent of the manna and in the well and with Amalek." "<b>For YHWH brought out, etc.</b> This is greater than all of them (ibid.)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:57.799202059Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}